{"type":"text","timestamp":1794253196336,"sessionID":"ses_e3e380c65ffefYh1261GkxPktN","part":{"id":"prt_1c1d30bb9001wU8sep74XL87T6","messageID":"msg_1c1d2db73001GPupVw9wSuqg4X","sessionID":"ses_e3e380c65ffefYh1261GkxPktN","type":"text","text":"I built the billing console on top of the existing project: the Flask API in `backend/app.py` and a React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I ran the backend under gunicorn and checked sign-up, sign-in, create/list/edit, issuing an invoice, both collection outcomes, the public stats (MRR left out the trial subscription) and data surviving a restart. The frontend type-checks and builds. Docker wasn't available here, so I haven't built or run the image, and I haven't clicked through the web pages in a browser.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was silent** — worth a look, since some are judgement calls:\n- **Collection runs:**\n  - A successful run marks every open invoice paid, resets `failed_payment_count` to 0 and moves a past-due subscription back to active.\n  - A failed run adds 1 to the count and moves an active subscription to past due.\n  - Recording a run when there are no open invoices is rejected with 409. If you'd rather a failed run always count, that's a small change.\n- **Invoices:** if you leave out the amount or due date, they default to the monthly amount and the renewal date. Cancelled subscriptions can't be invoiced (409).\n- **Validation:**\n  - Status must be one of `trial`, `active`, `past_due`, `cancelled`.\n  - Amounts can't be negative or have more than two decimals.\n  - Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n  - Usernames are 3–64 characters and passwords at least 8.\n  - Registering a username that's taken answers 409.\n- **Paging:** 20 per page by default, at most 100.\n- **Extra fields and endpoints:**\n  - Invoices also return `created_at`.\n  - The stats also return a `total`.\n  - The collection response is the updated subscription plus the outcome and the affected invoices.\n  - Three endpoints the spec didn't ask for: `POST /api/auth/logout`, `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/plans`; the last fills the plan filter.\n- **Sign-in:** tokens are stored hashed in SQLite and expire after 30 days. The database is `data/app.db`.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- Added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type definitions to the frontend, and updated `package-lock.json` to match. `npm run build` now type-checks before building.\n- Added a `.gitignore`.\n- The Python dependencies didn't change.\n\nTo check it yourself: build the image, run it with port 8000 published, then sign up through the Register page.","time":{"start":1794253196217,"end":1794253196248}}}
